<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Home for Winter Break: Rentals for College Students and Drivers 21 to 24</h1>
<p>Rent at 21 with no young-driver fee. Here&#x27;s what students home for break need to bring.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>Winter break means a few weeks at home: a holiday job, catching up with friends, a trip to see relatives, and the drive back to campus in January. If the family car is already spoken for, a rental gives you your own wheels without borrowing anyone's keys.</p>
<h2>Rent at 21, with no young-driver fee</h2>
<p>Our minimum renter age is <strong>21</strong>, and there's <strong>no under-25 fee</strong>. Drivers 21 to 24 can rent any vehicle in the fleet, including the minivan and the 15-passenger van. Many national chains add a daily young-renter surcharge. We don't. More on our <a href="/young-driver-car-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">young driver page</a>.</p>
<h2>What to bring</h2>
<ul>
<li>A valid U.S. driver's license in your name.</li>
<li>A credit or debit card (Visa, Mastercard, or Discover) linked to a checking account. No American Express and no checks.</li>
<li>Proof of full-coverage auto insurance showing the policy number and expiration date.</li>
</ul>
<p>A security deposit, starting at $300, is held separately from your rental charges. We'll confirm the exact amount when you book. If you're on a parent's insurance policy, bring that card and confirm with the agent that the coverage extends to a rental. Our <a href="/blog/does-car-insurance-cover-rental-car-wisconsin.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">insurance guide</a> lists the questions to ask.</p>
<h2>Pick the rate that fits a long break</h2>
<p>Break usually runs three to five weeks, so weekly rates are where the value is. For local renters, an intermediate car is $330/week and a full-size is $390/week, both with unlimited mileage. Non-local rates are intermediate $75/day or $450/week, full-size $85/day or $510/week, and SUV/AWD $100/day or $600/week, plus a per-mile charge. Call 715-396-1466 for the per-mile rate. Local means residents of Black River Falls and Jackson County, WI. Staying longer than a few weeks? Long-term rentals are quoted by phone.</p>
<h2>Heading back to campus with a carload?</h2>
<p>If the January drive back includes a winter's worth of new stuff, the <a href="/blog/7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> with the seats folded hauls a lot. It's $78/day plus $0.10/mile. See the <a href="/blog/college-move-in-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">college move-in guide</a> for packing tips.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> to reserve. Hours can change around Christmas and New Year's, so confirm pickup times when you book.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What is the minimum age to rent a car at Riverside Auto Rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>21. Drivers 21 to 24 can rent any vehicle in the fleet, and there is no under-25 fee.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is there a young-driver fee?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Riverside Auto Rental does not charge an under-25 or young-renter fee.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">I&#x27;m on my parents&#x27; car insurance. Can I still rent?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, if you can show proof of full-coverage auto insurance with the policy number and expiration date. Confirm with the agent that the policy extends to a rental vehicle.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What&#x27;s the best rate for a month-long winter break?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Weekly rates. For local renters, an intermediate car is $330/week and a full-size is $390/week with unlimited mileage. Longer stays are quoted by phone as long-term rentals.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
